- **On create.** The whole new relic must fit, including every required property.
- **On update.** The piece being saved (a property, a part, a link) is checked, and a required property cannot be cleared. A save that breaks the schema is refused with a message naming the rule.
- **On migrate.** The whole relic must fit the version it is moving to.
- **The not-conforming flag** is worked out for the whole relic when the local index picks up a change to it.
- **Never on read or sync.** A relic that does not fit its schema stays readable and is flagged as not conforming. This can happen after two valid edits meet, or when a teammate saved before syncing a newer schema.
- **Unknown version.** A relic that names a schema version this clone has not synced yet can be read. Editing it is refused until the clone syncs.

Anyone with push access can write to the repository without the Workbook command, so the schema guides honest tools. It is not a security boundary. The same is true of every other rule in Workbook.
